obo:BFO_0000001 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "001-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000001 rdf:type owl:Class .
obo:BFO_0000001 rdfs:label "entity"@en .
obo:BFO_0000001 skos:definition "(Elucidation) An entity is anything that exists or has existed or will exist"@en .
obo:BFO_0000001 skos:example "Julius Caesar; the Second World War; your body mass index; Verdi's Requiem"@en .

obo:BFO_0000002 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "008-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000002 owl:disjointWith obo:BFO_0000003 .
obo:BFO_0000002 rdf:type owl:Class .
obo:BFO_0000002 rdfs:label "continuant"@en .
obo:BFO_0000002 rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000001 .
obo:BFO_0000002 skos:definition "(Elucidation) A continuant is an entity that persists, endures, or continues to exist through time while maintaining its identity"@en .
obo:BFO_0000002 skos:example "A human being; a tennis ball; a cave; a region of space; someone's temperature"@en .

obo:BFO_0000003 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "077-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000003 rdf:type owl:Class .
obo:BFO_0000003 rdfs:label "occurrent"@en .
obo:BFO_0000003 rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000001 .
obo:BFO_0000003 skos:definition "(Elucidation) An occurrent is an entity that unfolds itself in time or it is the start or end of such an entity or it is a temporal or spatiotemporal region"@en .
obo:BFO_0000003 skos:example "As for process, history, process boundary, spatiotemporal region, zero-dimensional temporal region, one-dimensional temporal region, temporal interval, temporal instant."@en .

obo:BFO_0000004 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "017-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000004 rdf:type owl:Class .
obo:BFO_0000004 rdfs:label "independent continuant"@en .
obo:BFO_0000004 rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000002 .
obo:BFO_0000004 skos:definition "b is an independent continuant =Def b is a continuant & there is no c such that b specifically depends on c or b generically depends on c"@en .
obo:BFO_0000004 skos:example "An atom; a molecule; an organism; a heart; a chair; the bottom right portion of a human torso; a leg; the interior of your mouth; a spatial region; an orchestra"@en .

obo:BFO_0000015 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "083-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000015 rdf:type owl:Class .
obo:BFO_0000015 rdfs:label "process"@en .
obo:BFO_0000015 rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000003 .
obo:BFO_0000015 skos:altLabel "event"@en .
obo:BFO_0000015 skos:definition "(Elucidation) p is a process means p is an occurrent that has some temporal proper part and for some time t, p has some material entity as participant"@en .
obo:BFO_0000015 skos:example "An act of selling; the life of an organism; a process of sleeping; a process of cell-division; a beating of the heart; a process of meiosis; the taxiing of an aircraft; the programming of a computer"@en .

obo:BFO_0000017 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "058-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000017 owl:disjointWith obo:BFO_0000019 .
obo:BFO_0000017 rdf:type owl:Class .
obo:BFO_0000017 rdfs:label "realizable entity"@en .
obo:BFO_0000017 rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000020 .
obo:BFO_0000017 skos:definition "(Elucidation) A realizable entity is a specifically dependent continuant that inheres in some independent continuant which is not a spatial region & which is of a type some instances of which are realized in processes of a correlated type"@en .
obo:BFO_0000017 skos:example "The role of being a doctor; the role of this boundary to delineate where Utah and Colorado meet; the function of your reproductive organs; the disposition of your blood to coagulate; the disposition of this piece of metal to conduct electricity"@en .

obo:BFO_0000019 rdf:type owl:Class .
obo:BFO_0000019 rdfs:label "quality"@en .

obo:BFO_0000020 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "050-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000020 rdf:type owl:Class .
obo:BFO_0000020 rdfs:label "specifically dependent continuant"@en .
obo:BFO_0000020 rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000002 .
obo:BFO_0000020 skos:definition "b is a specifically dependent continuant =Def b is a continuant & there is some independent continuant c which is not a spatial region & which is such that b specifically depends on c"@en .
obo:BFO_0000020 skos:example "(with multiple bearers) John's love for Mary; the ownership relation between John and this statue; the relation of authority between John and his subordinates"@en .
obo:BFO_0000020 skos:example "(with one bearer) The mass of this tomato; the pink colour of a medium rare piece of grilled filet mignon at its centre; the smell of this portion of mozzarella; the disposition of this fish to decay; the role of being a doctor; the function of this heart to pump blood; the shape of this hole"@en .

obo:BFO_0000023 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "061-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000023 rdf:type owl:Class .
obo:BFO_0000023 rdfs:label "role"@en .
obo:BFO_0000023 rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000017 .
obo:BFO_0000023 skos:altLabel "externally-grounded realizable entity"@en .
obo:BFO_0000023 skos:definition "(Elucidation) A role b is a realizable entity such that b exists because there is some single bearer that is in some special physical, social, or institutional set of circumstances in which this bearer does not have to be & b is not such that, if it ceases to exist, then the physical make-up of the bearer is thereby changed"@en .
obo:BFO_0000023 skos:example "The priest role; the student role; the role of subject in a clinical trial; the role of a stone in marking a property boundary; the role of a boundary to demarcate two neighbouring administrative territories; the role of a building in serving as a military target"@en .

obo:BFO_0000027 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "025-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000027 rdf:type owl:Class .
obo:BFO_0000027 rdfs:label "object aggregate"@en .
obo:BFO_0000027 rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000040 .
obo:BFO_0000027 skos:definition "(Elucidation) An object aggregate is a material entity consisting exactly of a plurality (≥1) of objects as member parts which together form a unit"@en .
obo:BFO_0000027 skos:example "The aggregate of the musicians in a symphony orchestra and their instruments; the aggregate of bearings in a constant velocity axle joint; the nitrogen atoms in the atmosphere; a collection of cells in a blood biobank"@en .
obo:BFO_0000027 skos:scopeNote "'Exactly' means that there are no parts of the object aggregate other than its member parts." .
obo:BFO_0000027 skos:scopeNote "The unit can, at certain times, consist of exactly one object, for example, when a wolf litter loses all but one of its pups, but it must at some time have a plurality of member parts." .

obo:BFO_0000030 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "024-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000030 rdf:type owl:Class .
obo:BFO_0000030 rdfs:label "object"@en .
obo:BFO_0000030 rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000040 .
obo:BFO_0000030 skos:definition "(Elucidation) An object is a material entity which manifests causal unity & is of a type instances of which are maximal relative to the sort of causal unity manifested"@en .
obo:BFO_0000030 skos:example "An organism; a fish tank; a planet; a laptop; a valve; a block of marble; an ice cube"@en .
obo:BFO_0000030 skos:scopeNote "A description of three primary sorts of causal unity is provided in Basic Formal Ontology 2.0. Specification and User Guide"@en .

obo:BFO_0000031 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "074-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000031 rdf:type owl:Class .
obo:BFO_0000031 rdfs:label "generically dependent continuant"@en .
obo:BFO_0000031 rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000002 .
obo:BFO_0000031 skos:altLabel "g-dependent continuant"@en .
obo:BFO_0000031 skos:definition "(Elucidation) A generically dependent continuant is an entity that exists in virtue of the fact that there is at least one of what may be multiple copies which is the content or the pattern that multiple copies would share"@en .
obo:BFO_0000031 skos:example "The pdf file on your laptop; the pdf file that is a copy thereof on my laptop; the sequence of this protein molecule; the sequence that is a copy thereof in that protein molecule; the content that is shared by a string of dots and dashes written on a page and the transmitted Morse code signal; the content of a sentence; an engineering blueprint"@en .

obo:BFO_0000040 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "019-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000040 owl:disjointWith obo:BFO_0000141 .
obo:BFO_0000040 rdf:type owl:Class .
obo:BFO_0000040 rdfs:label "material entity"@en .
obo:BFO_0000040 rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000004 .
obo:BFO_0000040 skos:definition "(Elucidation) A material entity is an independent continuant has some portion of matter as continuant part"@en .
obo:BFO_0000040 skos:example "A human being; the undetached arm of a human being; an aggregate of human beings"@en .

obo:BFO_0000054 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "206-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000054 owl:inverseOf obo:BFO_0000055 .
obo:BFO_0000054 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .
obo:BFO_0000054 rdfs:domain obo:BFO_0000017 .
obo:BFO_0000054 rdfs:label "has realization"@en .
obo:BFO_0000054 rdfs:range obo:BFO_0000015 .
obo:BFO_0000054 skos:altLabel "realized in"@en .
obo:BFO_0000054 skos:definition "b has realization c =Def c realizes b"@en .
obo:BFO_0000054 skos:example "As for realizes"@en .

obo:BFO_0000055 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "059-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000055 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .
obo:BFO_0000055 rdfs:domain obo:BFO_0000015 .
obo:BFO_0000055 rdfs:label "realizes"@en .
obo:BFO_0000055 rdfs:range obo:BFO_0000017 .
obo:BFO_0000055 skos:definition "(Elucidation) realizes is a relation between a process b and realizable entity c such that c inheres in some d & for all t, if b has participant d then c exists & the type instantiated by b is correlated with the type instantiated by c"@en .
obo:BFO_0000055 skos:example "A balding process realizes a disposition to go bald; a studying process realizes a student role; a process of pumping blood realizes the pumping function of a heart"@en .
obo:BFO_0000055 skos:scopeNote "Users that require more sophisticated representations of time are encouraged to import a temporal extension of BFO-Core provided by the BFO development team. See documentation for guidance: <Link>"@en .

obo:BFO_0000056 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "250-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000056 owl:inverseOf obo:BFO_0000057 .
obo:BFO_0000056 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .
obo:BFO_0000056 rdfs:label "participates in"@en .
obo:BFO_0000056 rdfs:range obo:BFO_0000015 .
obo:BFO_0000056 skos:definition "(Elucidation) participates in holds between some b that is either a specifically dependent continuant or generically dependent continuant or independent continuant that is not a spatial region & some process p such that b participates in p some way"@en .
obo:BFO_0000056 skos:scopeNote "Users that require more sophisticated representations of time are encouraged to import a temporal extension of BFO-Core provided by the BFO development team. See documentation for guidance: <Link>"@en .
obo:BFO_0000056 skos:scopeNote "Users that require more sophisticated representations of time are encouraged to import a temporal extension of BFO-Core provided by the BFO development team. See documentation for guidance: <https://github.com/BFO-ontology/BFO-2020/tree/master/src/owl/profiles/temporal%20extensions>"@en .

obo:BFO_0000057 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "248-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000057 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .
obo:BFO_0000057 rdfs:domain obo:BFO_0000015 .
obo:BFO_0000057 rdfs:label "has participant"@en .
obo:BFO_0000057 skos:definition "p has participant c =Def c participates in p"@en .
obo:BFO_0000057 skos:scopeNote "Users that require more sophisticated representations of time are encouraged to import a temporal extension of BFO-Core provided by the BFO development team. See documentation for guidance: <Link>"@en .
obo:BFO_0000057 skos:scopeNote "Users that require more sophisticated representations of time are encouraged to import a temporal extension of BFO-Core provided by the BFO development team. See documentation for guidance: <https://github.com/BFO-ontology/BFO-2020/tree/master/src/owl/profiles/temporal%20extensions>"@en .

obo:BFO_0000062 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "213-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000062 owl:inverseOf obo:BFO_0000063 .
obo:BFO_0000062 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .
obo:BFO_0000062 rdf:type owl:TransitiveProperty .
obo:BFO_0000062 rdfs:domain obo:BFO_0000003 .
obo:BFO_0000062 rdfs:label "preceded by"@en .
obo:BFO_0000062 rdfs:range obo:BFO_0000003 .
obo:BFO_0000062 skos:definition "b preceded by c =Def b precedes c"@en .
obo:BFO_0000062 skos:example "The temporal region occupied by the second half of the match is preceded by the temporal region occupied by the first half of the match"@en .

obo:BFO_0000063 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "270-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000063 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .
obo:BFO_0000063 rdf:type owl:TransitiveProperty .
obo:BFO_0000063 rdfs:domain obo:BFO_0000003 .
obo:BFO_0000063 rdfs:label "precedes"@en .
obo:BFO_0000063 rdfs:range obo:BFO_0000003 .
obo:BFO_0000063 skos:definition "(Elucidation) precedes is a relation between occurrents o, o' such that if t is the temporal extent of o & t' is the temporal extent of o' then either the last instant of o is before the first instant of o' or the last instant of o is the first instant of o' & neither o nor o' are temporal instants"@en .
obo:BFO_0000063 skos:example "The temporal region occupied by Mary's birth precedes the temporal region occupied by Mary's death."@en .
obo:BFO_0000063 skos:scopeNote "Each temporal region is its own temporal extent. The temporal extent of a spatiotemporal region is the temporal region it temporally projects onto. The temporal extent of a process or process boundary that occupies temporal region t is t." .
obo:BFO_0000063 skos:scopeNote "Precedes defines a strict partial order on occurrents." .

obo:BFO_0000117 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "202-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000117 owl:inverseOf obo:BFO_0000132 .
obo:BFO_0000117 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .
obo:BFO_0000117 rdf:type owl:TransitiveProperty .
obo:BFO_0000117 rdfs:domain obo:BFO_0000003 .
obo:BFO_0000117 rdfs:label "has occurrent part"@en .
obo:BFO_0000117 rdfs:range obo:BFO_0000003 .
obo:BFO_0000117 skos:definition "b has occurrent part c =Def c occurrent part of b"@en .
obo:BFO_0000117 skos:example "Mary's life has occurrent part Mary's 5th birthday"@en .

obo:BFO_0000132 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "003-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000132 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .
obo:BFO_0000132 rdf:type owl:TransitiveProperty .
obo:BFO_0000132 rdfs:domain obo:BFO_0000003 .
obo:BFO_0000132 rdfs:label "occurrent part of"@en .
obo:BFO_0000132 rdfs:range obo:BFO_0000003 .
obo:BFO_0000132 skos:definition "(Elucidation) occurrent part of is a relation between occurrents b and c when b is part of c"@en .
obo:BFO_0000132 skos:example "Mary's 5th birthday is an occurrent part of Mary's life; the first set of the tennis match is an occurrent part of the tennis match"@en .

obo:BFO_0000141 rdf:type owl:Class .
obo:BFO_0000141 rdfs:label "immaterial entity"@en .

obo:BFO_0000194 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "260-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000194 owl:inverseOf obo:BFO_0000195 .
obo:BFO_0000194 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .
obo:BFO_0000194 rdfs:label "specifically depended on by"@en .
obo:BFO_0000194 rdfs:range obo:BFO_0000020 .
obo:BFO_0000194 skos:altLabel "s-depended on by"@en .
obo:BFO_0000194 skos:definition "b specifically depended on by c =Def c specifically depends on b"@en .
obo:BFO_0000194 skos:example "Coloured object specifically depended on by colour"@en .

obo:BFO_0000195 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "012-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000195 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .
obo:BFO_0000195 rdfs:domain obo:BFO_0000020 .
obo:BFO_0000195 rdfs:label "specifically depends on"@en .
obo:BFO_0000195 skos:altLabel "s-depends on"@en .
obo:BFO_0000195 skos:definition "(Elucidation) specifically depends on is a relation between a specifically dependent continuant b and specifically dependent continuant or independent continuant that is not a spatial region c such that b and c share no parts in common & b is of a nature such that at all times t it cannot exist unless c exists & b is not a boundary of c"@en .
obo:BFO_0000195 skos:example "A shape specifically depends on the shaped object; hue, saturation and brightness of a colour sample specifically depends on each other"@en .
obo:BFO_0000195 skos:scopeNote "The analogue of specifically depends on for occurrents is has participant."@en .

obo:BFO_0000196 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "053-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000196 owl:inverseOf obo:BFO_0000197 .
obo:BFO_0000196 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .
obo:BFO_0000196 rdfs:label "bearer of"@en .
obo:BFO_0000196 rdfs:range obo:BFO_0000020 .
obo:BFO_0000196 rdfs:subPropertyOf obo:BFO_0000194 .
obo:BFO_0000196 skos:definition "b bearer of c =Def c inheres in b"@en .
obo:BFO_0000196 skos:example "A patch of ink is the bearer of a colour quality; an organism is the bearer of a temperature quality"@en .

obo:BFO_0000197 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "051-BFO" .
obo:BFO_0000197 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .
obo:BFO_0000197 rdfs:domain obo:BFO_0000020 .
obo:BFO_0000197 rdfs:label "inheres in"@en .
obo:BFO_0000197 rdfs:subPropertyOf obo:BFO_0000195 .
obo:BFO_0000197 skos:definition "b inheres in c =Def b is a specifically dependent continuant & c is an independent continuant that is not a spatial region & b specifically depends on c"@en .
obo:BFO_0000197 skos:example "A shape inheres in a shaped object; a mass inheres in a material entity"@en .
